name 'iterating-with-ai-preassessment-q5_2025'

question 'When is a `while` loop more appropriate than a `for` loop?'

wrong 'When you want the code to run as fast as possible.'
right 'When you need to repeat an action based on a condition that might change at any time (e.g., until a user clicks "Stop").'
wrong 'When you are working with an array of a fixed size.'
wrong 'When you want to ensure the loop only runs exactly five times.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 3

`while` loops (condition-controlled) are used when the number of repetitions isn't known beforehand and depends on a dynamic state or condition.
MARKDOWN
